  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+5t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-4{t}^{2}+t+1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86{t}^{2}+6t+5,\\,8{t}^{3}-8t+1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+6t+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-8t+1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e812t+6,\\,24{t}^{2}-8\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =\u27e812(0)+6,\\,24(0)-8\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86,\\,-8\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|\u27e86,\\,-8\u27e9| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
